  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 16-layer alternating HfO2/SiO2 stack on silicon substrate with air incidence. Initialize all layer thicknesses at quarter-wave optical thickness for 10500 nm center wavelength (HfO2 and SiO2 refractive indices at 10500 nm), then apply ±12% random perturbation to each layer. Use L-BFGS-B optimizer with thickness bounds 200-1800 nm per layer. Evaluate coherent TMM across 3000-13000 nm wavelength range at normal incidence. Objective: maximize weighted absorptance (high weight 8000-13000 nm, low weight 3000-5000 nm). Total layers fixed at 16, alternating HfO2/SiO2 sequence starting with HfO2 at air interface. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 3000-5000 nm, 8000-13000 nm. soft objectives: high emissivity in 8000-13000 nm; low emissivity in 3000-5000 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high emissivity in 3000-5000 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count not exceeding 24.",
